---
// Text Diff Tool — line-based diff between two blocks of text (a baseline
// config vs. what's currently running, two exported log windows, a script
// before and after an obfuscation layer was stripped), entirely client-side
// (src/utils/textDiff.ts — a from-scratch LCS diff, no dependency). Same
// page shape as the Hash Calculator / IOC Extractor (intro aside ->
// interactive tool -> reference notes). Static page — prerender to HTML
// served from the CDN.
export const prerender = true;
import { css } from 'styled-system/css';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import TextDiffTool from '../../components/TextDiffTool.astro';
import { toolChip } from '../../components/RelatedTools.astro';
import ExternalResources from '../../components/ExternalResources.astro';
import { EXTERNAL_RESOURCES } from '../../data/externalResources';
import { MAX_DIFF_LINES } from '../../utils/textDiff';

const sectionH2 = css({
  display: 'flex',
  alignItems: 'center',
  gap: '0.6rem',
  fontSize: '1.3rem',
  fontWeight: 700,
  mt: '2.5rem',
  mb: '1rem',
  pt: '1.5rem',
  borderTop: '1px solid token(colors.border)',
  scrollMarginTop: '90px',
});
const relatedList = css({ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '0.85rem' });
const relatedReason = css({ color: 'textMuted', fontSize: '0.85rem', mt: '0.35rem', lineHeight: 1.6 });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Text Diff Tool"
  description="Compare two blocks of text — logs, configs, scripts — and see exactly which lines were added, removed, or left unchanged. A from-scratch line-based diff, entirely in your browser, nothing uploaded."
>
  <PageHeader
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Tool Catalog', href: '/tools/' }, { label: 'Text Diff Tool' }]}
    eyebrow="Converters"
    title="Text Diff Tool"
    description="Paste a baseline and a current version of the same text and see exactly what changed, line by line — entirely local."
  />

  <aside
    class={css({
      bg: 'bgSubtle',
      border: '1px solid token(colors.border)',
      borderLeftWidth: '3px',
      borderLeftColor: 'primary',
      borderRadius: 'md',
      p: '1rem 1.25rem',
      mb: '1.5rem',
    })}
  >
    <p class={css({ color: 'text', lineHeight: 1.7, fontSize: '0.95rem', m: 0 })}>
      The diff runs on a from-scratch implementation of the same longest-common-subsequence approach behind{' '}
      <code class={css({ fontFamily: 'mono', fontSize: '0.88em', color: 'primary' })}>diff</code>/
      <code class={css({ fontFamily: 'mono', fontSize: '0.88em', color: 'primary' })}>git diff</code> — entirely in
      your browser, so nothing you paste on either side is ever transmitted anywhere. Each side is capped at{' '}
      {MAX_DIFF_LINES.toLocaleString()} lines to keep that comparison fast and local; a pasted input over that cap
      is compared using only its first {MAX_DIFF_LINES.toLocaleString()} lines, and the diff view flags it.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <p class={css({ color: 'text', lineHeight: 1.8, fontSize: '1rem', mb: '1.5rem' })}>
    A surprising amount of DFIR work comes down to "what's different between these two things." Two exports of
    the same log source, taken an hour apart — did anything get appended, or quietly pruned? Two copies of a
    startup script or scheduled task, one from a known-good host and one from a suspect one — which lines did an
    attacker actually touch? A "before" and "after" of a config file bracketing an incident window? Reading two
    blobs of text side by side and spotting every difference by eye doesn't scale past a handful of lines — this
    tool does that comparison for you and highlights exactly what changed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tool" class={css({ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', gap: '0.6rem', fontSize: '1.3rem', fontWeight: 700, mb: '1rem', scrollMarginTop: '90px' })}>
    <Icon name="columns" size={20} class={css({ color: 'primary' })} /> Compare
  </h2>
  <TextDiffTool />

  <h2 id="how-it-works" class={sectionH2}>
    <Icon name="book-open" size={20} class={css({ color: 'primary' })} /> Reading the diff
  </h2>
  <p class={css({ color: 'textMuted', fontSize: '0.9rem', lineHeight: 1.75, m: 0 })}>
    Every line is classified against the other side: unchanged lines are shown for context, a line only present in
    <strong class={css({ color: 'text' })}> Baseline</strong> is marked removed, and a line only present in
    <strong class={css({ color: 'text' })}> Current</strong> is marked added. A single edited line therefore shows
    up as a removed/added pair rather than an in-place change — matching that classification happens at the line
    level, not automatically merging an edit into one row, which keeps it fast and matches how most log and config
    comparisons actually get read. When a removed line and an added line pair up this way, a second word-level pass
    highlights exactly which words within that line changed, so a one-word edit reads as one highlighted word, not
    an entire line marked as different. The gutter on each row carries that line's number in whichever side(s) it
    appears in, so you can jump straight to the matching spot in the original file.
  </p>

  <h2 id="related" class={sectionH2}>
    <Icon name="wrench" size={20} class={css({ color: 'primary' })} /> Related tools
  </h2>
  <div class={relatedList}>
    <div>
      <a href="/tools/hash-calculator/" class={toolChip}>
        <Icon name="hash" size={13} /> Hash Calculator <Icon name="arrow-right" size={13} />
      </a>
      <p class={relatedReason}>
        Hash both versions first — if the hashes match, there's nothing to diff; if they don't, this tool shows you
        exactly where they diverge.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/tools/deobfuscator/" class={toolChip}>
        <Icon name="key" size={13} /> Codec Builder <Icon name="arrow-right" size={13} />
      </a>
      <p class={relatedReason}>
        Comparing two versions of an obfuscated script? Peel each one back here first, then diff the cleaned-up
        output instead of the encoded blob.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/tools/ioc-extractor/" class={toolChip}>
        <Icon name="alert-triangle" size={13} /> IOC Extractor <Icon name="arrow-right" size={13} />
      </a>
      <p class={relatedReason}>
        Once a diff surfaces the new lines in a log export, run just that added content through the extractor to
        pull out any indicators it introduced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ExternalResources resources={EXTERNAL_RESOURCES['text-diff']} />
</BaseLayout>
